:{"best":35,"brilliant":1,"great":3},"b":{"mistake":1,"best":35}},"moment":{"name":"10.Bxf7+","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","fen":"r3kb1r/ppq1pBpp/1np2n2/8/3P2b1/2N2N2/PPPBQPPP/R3K2R b KQkq - 0 10","from":"b3","to":"f7"},"finalFen":"4N3/2r5/5k1P/3n4/3R1PP1/1P6/1K6/8 b - - 6 66"},"white":"jefferyx","black":"Hikaru","labels":["book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","excellent","excellent","good","best","mistake","brilliant","best","great","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","inaccuracy","good","best","good","best","excellent","best","best","excellent","excellent","best","excellent","best","great","best","best","inaccuracy","best","best","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","good","inaccuracy","good","good","excellent","best","best","excellent","excellent","good","great","best","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","good","best","best","best","excellent","best","excellent","best","best","best","forced","best","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","excellent","best","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","excellent","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","best","excellent","best","good","good","best","best","good","excellent","best","best","best","best","forced","best","best","best","excellent","best","good","best"],"moments":[{"ply":18,"name":"9…Bg4","cls":"mistake","color":"b","headline":"9…Bg4 is a mistake: Black's winning chances go from 39% to 21%.","points":["White answers 10.Bxf7+, which takes the pawn on f7.","Better was 9…e6 (+1.24), which opens a line for the bishop on f8."],"better":"9…e6 opens a line for the bishop on f8. After 10.Ne4 Nxe4 11.Qxe4 Be7 12.O-O a5, the knights are traded (+1.24)."},{"ply":19,"name":"10.Bxf7+","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","headline":"10.Bxf7+!! A real sacrifice: White gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Puts the bishop on f7 where it can be taken.","Black can take, but after 10…Kxf7 11.Ne5+ Ke8 12.Nxg4 the engine rates it +3.89.","Takes the pawn on f7.","Leaves Black with an isolated pawn on e7: a long-term weakness.","10.Bxf7+ leaves Black with an isolated pawn on e7 and takes the f7 pawn.","Takes the f7 pawn."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"10.Bxf7+!! offers the bishop on f7. Taking it gives White the material back and more."},{"title":"What White gives up","text":"10.Bxf7+ puts the bishop on f7 where it can be taken by the king. That's a bishop on offer."},{"title":"If Black takes the bishop","text":"10…Kxf7 is met by 11.Ne5+. Then 12.Nxg4 takes the bishop on g4, and 13.Qxg4 takes the knight on g4. White ends up a pawn ahead: White is winning (+3.50). This is Black's best try."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 10.Qe5, is clearly weaker (+0.78 against +3.89). Black answers 10…Qd7. That would leave White a little better."}]},{"ply":21,"name":"11.Ne5+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"11.Ne5+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Plants the knight on e5: a pawn defends it and no enemy pawn can chase it away.","Moving away uncovers the queen on e2, which now hits the bishop on g4.","The next best move, 11.O-O-O, would drop White's winning chances from 79% to 23% (−3.29).","11.Ne5+ wins a knight, picking it up with 12.Nxg4.","Sets up a sequence and wins a knight once the captures settle, picking it up with 12.Nxg4.","Black answers 11…Ke8."]},{"ply":43,"name":"22.Nxd5","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"22.Nxd5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the knight on d5.","The next best move, 22.Ne4, would drop White's winning chances from 81% to 63% (+1.39).","22.Nxd5 wins a pawn.","Takes the knight on d5 and wins a pawn once the captures settle.","Black answers 22…cxd5, taking back and taking e4 away from the rook on e1.","After 22…cxd5 23.Bxe7 Re8 24.h3 Qxh4 25.Bxh4 Rxe1+ 26.Nxe1 Rh6, the queens come off, the rooks are traded and White comes out a pawn up (+3.67)."]},{"ply":65,"name":"33.Rxh7","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"33.Rxh7! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the rook on h7.","The next best move, 33.Rfc7, would drop White's winning chances from 90% to 47% (−0.35).","33.Rxh7 trades off the attacked rook instead of losing it to …Rxf7.","Black was threatening …Rxf7, winning a rook. The rook takes something with it instead.","Trades rooks: trading pieces when ahead brings the win closer.","The rook on h7 can be taken by the knight on f8 or the king."]}],"opening":{"name":"Scandinavian Defense: Main Line","eco":"B01","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 7.Nf3: 13 moves in all, 7 by White and 6 by Black.","Black left the book with 7…Nbd7. In 30 games from this position, strong players played 7…Bg4 (50%) or 7…Bf5 (40%).","From here White scored 78% in those games, with 8% drawn."]}}